meta {
  name: what listed transcripts contain
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/claude/transcripts/facts
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  ~path: {{transcriptPath}}
}

docs {
  What a bounded batch of listed transcripts contains, so the import dialog can label a row without reading the store. Answers {maxBatch, facts: [{path, models, workflowCalls, subagents, language?, firstPrompt?}]}. Models are listed in the order they first spoke; subagents are counted from the session's sidecar folder, not the transcript. Unknown facts are omitted rather than sent as a placeholder. At most 24 paths per call; a path outside the store, a non-.jsonl name and a missing file all yield no row.
  
  Fence: host — Loopback fence: the TCP peer must be loopback AND the Host header must be localhost/127.0.0.1/::1. A REST client passes automatically when it targets http://localhost:<port>. A LAN IP or rebound DNS name in the URL answers a blank 404.
  
  Writes state: no
}
